ons.\\n   - Evidence: scripts refer to `workspace/`, `workspace/script`, `output/store/query_index`, `report/...`.\\n   - Risk: running them directly in the new project may write to wrong places or fail.\\n   - Recommended next action: port only selected scripts into a clean current development task; do not execute old scripts in-place.\\n\\n## Medium Priority Gaps\\n\\n5. `main.py` conflicts with the modern package entry.\\n   - Evidence: `main.py` defines lowercase `pxfquery` class with many `pass` methods; `core.py` defines modern `PxFquery`.\\n   - Risk: confusing future developers and packaging users.\\n   - Recommended next action: mark `main.py` obsolete or exclude it when creating the current package.\\n\\n6. Validation reports conflict in authority and naming.\\n   - Evidence: latest report index says one Act-1 validation path is an auth-failure record, while migrated `M-0255` has successful examples.\\n   - Risk: evidence can be overstated if old report copies are read without index priority.\\n   - Recommended next action: keep a canonical validation evidence table and rerun minimal current smoke tests.\\n\\n7. Reverse query is implemented but less deeply validated than forward resolver.\\n   - Evidence: Act-1 report includes one reverse example; most matrix/suite evidence is forward-focused.\\n   - Risk: reverse-query manuscript claims may be weaker.\\n   - Recommended next action: add deterministic reverse smoke cases after package setup.\\n\\n8. Drug generic-query behavior is inconsistent.\\n   - Evidence: suite reports show EGFR inhibitor and erlotinib cases can be `PROXY_PERT` in one run but `NOT_FOUND` in another.\\n   - Risk: natural-language drug examples may fail during demo.\\n   - Recommended next action: choose exact drug-name examples for manuscript demos until fallback behavior is stabilized.\\n\\n## Lower Priority Or Deferred\\n\\n9. Zenodo/download support is planned but not implemented.\\n   - Evidence: `DataLoader.download_zenodo()` raises `NotImplementedError`.\\n   - Risk: not blocking local manuscript workflow, but affects distribution polish.\\n   - Recommendation: defer until core local workflow passes.\\n\\n10. Plotting exists but is not validated as manuscript-ready figures.\\n    - Evidence: `viz/plots.py` exists, but T007 did not find current figure QA.\\n    - Risk: figures may need polish for Genes submission.\\n    - Recommendation: create a later figure task after query outputs are stable.\\n\\n11. Large matrices and embeddings remain raw migrated assets.\\n    - Evidence: flat library records many large data files, some originally migrated as large assets.\\n    - Risk: accidental expensive loading or provenance confusion.\\n    - Recommendation: register only the exact matrix/index assets needed by each development task.\\n\\n## Claims To Avoid\\n\\n- Do not claim PxFquery is a stable broad AI-agent system.\\n- Do not claim natural-language resolver performance is stable across all biological domains.\\n- Do not claim old validation reports are manuscript-ready current-project validation.\\n- Do not claim full distribution/download support exists.\\n\\n## Safer Claims\\n\\n- PxFquery has a deterministic LINCS/CMAP functional query core.\\n- It supports forward and reverse query primitives over functional score matrices.\\n- It has evidence-aware exact/proxy retrieval logic using cell-line, gene, drug, and function indexes.\\n- LLMs can assist parsing and summarization, but deterministic retrieval is the scientific foundation.\",\"lineStart\":1,\"lineEnd\":78,\"totalLines\":78,\"truncated\":false}},\"title\":\"3_phase_digestion/goal_development_asset_digestion/task_digest_pxfquery_development_state/4_artifact/2_persist/pxfquery_development_gap_and_risk_list_v20260617.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1782361325247,\"end\":1782361325255}},\"id\":\"prt_efd037eb90014r1hQBM8YIsqvZ\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_102fe5ea0ffe8FbRea9F4mAlkE\",\"messageID\":\"msg_efd02bc6b001KiX68yN8qQoVGP\"}}\n"}, "quarantine